 "docs": {
  "en": {
   "title": "US West snow outlook to 30 November: 54 in at Kingvale, 53 in at Mt. Shasta Ski Park",
   "description": "The two-week picture in the US West, 17 November to 30 November, drawn from the two global models that reach two weeks, ECMWF and GFS. Middle of the …",
   "lede": "The two-week picture in the US West, 17 November to 30 November, drawn from the two global models that reach two weeks, ECMWF and GFS. Middle of the two on the maps, low and high of the two in the text: that is the rule of this daily series. The most goes to Kingvale: about 54 in (136 cm) on its upper slopes, 33 in (84 cm)–74 in (188 cm) depending on the model, then Mt. Shasta Ski Park with 53 in (134 cm). Every number here is an estimate with some uncertainty; the trend over several days is usually more reliable than one value.",
   "sections": [
    {
     "h": "Resort by resort, the next 14 days",
     "p": [
      "Kingvale (United States): about 54 in (136 cm) in 14 days (33 in (84 cm)–74 in (188 cm) between the models), 36 in (92 cm) in the first week and 17 in (44 cm) in the second. Mark 19 November: that is the biggest day, with 16 in (40 cm), out of 7 days at 5 cm or more.",
      "Mt. Shasta Ski Park (United States): about 53 in (134 cm) in 14 days (32 in (82 cm)–73 in (186 cm) between the models), 28 in (70 cm) in the first week and 25 in (64 cm) in the second. Mark 18 November: that is the biggest day, with 15 in (37 cm), out of 6 days at 5 cm or more.",
      "At Palisades Tahoe Olympic Valley (United States) the two weeks add up to about 50 in (128 cm) (35 in (88 cm)–66 in (168 cm) depending on the model): 33 in (83 cm) by the end of the first week, then 18 in (45 cm) more. Mark 19 November: that is the biggest day, with 15 in (37 cm), out of 7 days at 5 cm or more.",
      "Bear Valley (United States): about 49 in (124 cm) in 14 days (34 in (87 cm)–63 in (161 cm) between the models), 34 in (87 cm) in the first week and 15 in (37 cm) in the second. Mark 19 November: that is the biggest day, with 19 in (47 cm), out of 5 days at 5 cm or more.",
      "At Badger Pass (United States) the two weeks add up to about 47 in (119 cm) (33 in (83 cm)–61 in (155 cm) depending on the model): 37 in (93 cm) by the end of the first week, then 10 in (26 cm) more. The snowiest day is 19 November with 21 in (54 cm); 6 days bring 5 cm or more.",
      "At China Peak (United States) the two weeks add up to about 46 in (117 cm) (31 in (80 cm)–61 in (155 cm) depending on the model): 36 in (92 cm) by the end of the first week, then 10 in (25 cm) more. The snowiest day is 19 November with 22 in (56 cm); 6 days bring 5 cm or more."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "The snow still to come",
     "p": [
      "Up to 27 in (69 cm) of new snow is forecast at Kingvale over the next days.",
      "Forecasts move: the timing is usually more reliable than the totals, so check again two days before you go.",
      "At about 7,034 ft (2,144 m), Kingvale has 6 in (16 cm) today; a normal 16 November has 2 in (4 cm) there.",
      "Only one winter in ten has more than 17 in (42 cm) on this date.",
      "A week ago the same spot had 0 in (0 cm).",
      "In past winters the best snow at Kingvale usually came early March / mid-March."
     ]
    },
    {
